# What `git archive` ships to the droplet.
#
# deploy/DROPLET_SETUP.md deploys with `git archive HEAD | ssh ... tar -x`,
# which shipped 47.5 MB every time and, worse, OVERWROTE the droplet's own
# data/mars_history.db with whatever happened to be on the deploying laptop.
# The droplet runs USE_SNOWFLAKE=1 and never reads that file, so the overwrite
# has been harmless -- "has been" is not a guarantee, and 39.5 MB over SSH to
# clobber a file nothing opens is not a thing to keep doing.
#
# export-ignore affects `git archive` ONLY. Streamlit Community Cloud clones
# the repo, so the dashboard still gets everything it needs.
#
# data/mars_roster.json IS NOT EXCLUDED AND MUST NOT BE. update_index.py line
# 464 does json.loads(ROSTER_PATH.read_text()) unconditionally -- it is the
# roster of ~60 sale barns the whole reconstruction walks, and without it the
# 07:45 run dies on a missing file. A blanket `data/ export-ignore` was the
# obvious change here and it would have taken the pipeline out.
#
# 47.5 MB -> 1.9 MB.

data/mars_history.db export-ignore
data/*.xlsx export-ignore
